messages:
jamie_design: quick note from today's desk check — Compact models list has a keyboard focus oddity: when you tab fast the focus ring flickers and sometimes the previous row's ring stays for a frame. dark theme looks worse. :thinking:

pierre_ui: can repro on Chrome. I think it's the hover scale + focus outline both animating. We applied the same transform for hover and focus which wasn't intentional.

linda_a11y: repro steps: Console → Models → Density: Compact → tab rapidly through rows. Observed on Win Chrome + NVDA: sometimes NVDA reads previous row again. Also saw that some empty cells have tabindex=0 which creates extra focus stops.

pierre_ui: plan: scope the scale/box-shadow to :hover only, and use :focus-visible (no transform) for keyboard focus. Proposed CSS snippet:
```css
.models-row:focus-visible {
  transform: none;
  box-shadow: none;
  outline: 3px solid var(--focus-accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
.models-row:hover {
  transform: scale(1.01);
  transition: transform 120ms ease;
}
```

linda_a11y: good. Also remove tabindex from non-interactive children — only the row should be tabbable. For status changes (Queued → Training) add `role="status" aria-live="polite"` and include readable text like "Status: training" so SR users hear it.

devops_bot: note about skiplink: skip-to-content currently lands under the sticky header on small screens. Recommend adding `:target { scroll-margin-top: var(--site-header-height); }` or `html { scroll-padding-top: var(--site-header-height); }` so the first row isn't hidden.

aria_bot: accessibility-linter: create ticket A11Y-331. Rules suggested: no transform on :focus-visible, focus contrast >= 4.5:1 for small targets, no redundant tabindex in row children, skiplink landing offset, aria-live for status updates.

pierre_ui: I'll open a small PR today with the CSS and DOM tabindex cleanup. I'll include a unit test that simulates keyboard tabbing sequence for the first 10 rows and an integration note for the a11y QA.

linda_a11y: I'll review the PR and run NVDA/VoiceOver checks once it's on staging. QA script I will use: 1) Keyboard only: Tab/Shift-Tab across first 20 rows, verify single focus per row; 2) SR: confirm row announces "Model name, Status: X" once; 3) Skiplink: trigger skip and ensure first row visible; 4) Status update: confirm polite SR announcement.

jamie_design: perfect — thanks. Let's get this in before we flip Compact default. :thumbsup:
